# Sinfonia 11 in G minor, BWV 797 (3/8, 72 bars)
#
# Character: a gentle, singing piece in a flowing 3/8, closer to a
# lyrical song than a dance. Long held notes in each voice against a
# falling sixteenth-note figure; it should breathe, not drive.
#
# Tempo: dotted quarter = 36 (eighth = 108), about two minutes.
# Basis: Angela Hewitt (Hyperion, 1994) 1:59, about 36 bars a minute;
# Andras Schiff (ECM, clavichord) 1:55, about 37.6. Glenn Gould (1964)
# is far slower (3:45, about 19 bars a minute) and was not followed.
# Durations from retailer and artist track lists, so approximate.
#
# Structure (from the Mutopia score):
#   1-8    Subject in the top (head: rest, d-bes-g, leap up, then long
#          falling notes), answer in the mid on D from bar 2, while the
#          bass plays its own countersubject. Cadence in G minor, bar 8.
#   8-16   Subject in the bass (bar 8), then the head passed between
#          the voices (mid 9 and 12, top 11 and 14) through C minor to a
#          cadence in B-flat major, bar 16.
#   17-23  Close imitation of the head, one voice per bar, falling by
#          step (E-flat, C minor, B-flat, toward D minor).
#   24-29  Dominant pedal on A in the bass (24-28), building to D minor.
#   30-36  Bars 2-7 restated note for note at the same pitch (mid has
#          the answer again), then a cadence in D minor, bar 36.
#   37-48  Rising arpeggio sequence in the bass (37-40), falling
#          sequence (41-45), cadence in G minor, bar 48.
#   48-56  Subject in the bass (bar 48), sequence toward D.
#   57-64  Dominant pedal on D in the bass (57-63): the climax, with the
#          top pausing on F-sharp in 63-64.
#   65-72  Bars 1-8 return unchanged (top, then mid at 66); final
#          cadence in G minor.

tempo 36 4.           # dotted quarter, see above

dyn 1 mp              # bars 1-16: exposition, quiet and singing
lead 1-2 top          # bars 1-2: subject in the top
lead 2-4 mid          # bars 2-4: answer in the mid, on D
lead 8-10 bottom      # bars 8-10: subject in the bass, after the G minor cadence

dyn 17 mf             # bars 17-23: after the B-flat cadence, close imitation, fuller
ramp 24-29 f          # bars 24-29: the A pedal builds toward D minor

dyn 30 p              # bars 30-36: bars 2-7 come back unchanged, so play them as an echo
lead 30-32 mid        # bars 30-32: the answer in the mid again

dyn 37 mf             # bars 37-56: after the D minor cadence, the rising sequence
lead 48-50 bottom     # bars 48-50: subject in the bass, after the G minor cadence

ramp 57-63 f          # bars 57-63: D pedal, the climax of the piece
broaden 64 0.92       # bar 64: a breath on the dominant before the return

dyn 65 mf             # bars 65-72: the opening returns, a step stronger than at first
lead 65-66 top        # bars 65-66: subject in the top once more

rit 4 0.7             # last 4 bars (short 3/8 bars) into the final G minor cadence
